  <wpt lat="44.112005" lon="-72.855947">
    <name>Mad River (above Warren Village)</name>
    <desc>BKT | B1 | Mad River watershed | REPORT COORDINATE PROBLEM: Table 11 gives 44.175722, -72.661631, which lands in the Dog River valley about 10 miles east — almost certainly a transcription error. Plotted at Warren village instead; say this in the popup. Report: the upper Mad above Warren Village has excellent high-gradient forested habitat and some of the highest trout numbers in the watershed, mostly wild brookies with occasional rainbows, managed for wild trout. Below Warren, warmer water and habitat limit trout to big pools and tributary mouths; rainbows stocked from Warren to the Moretown 8 dam; dams in Warren and Moretown fragment habitat. | Nearest access: Warren village - covered bridge / Main St (31 m, 13.8 min); Warren Falls lot (3919 Rte 100) (38 m, 15.9 min); Moss Glen Falls pull-off (Granville Gulf, Rte 100) (2316 m, 25.8 min) | Source: VFWD 2017, Table 11 p.7 https://dec.vermont.gov/sites/dec/files/wsm/mapp/docs/mp_UpperWinooskiWatershedFisheriesSummary_2017-12-15.pdf#page=7 | Confidence: low (Google Places (Warren village) — report coordinate rejected) | Drive from inn: 13.6 min</desc>
    <link href="https://dec.vermont.gov/sites/dec/files/wsm/mapp/docs/mp_UpperWinooskiWatershedFisheriesSummary_2017-12-15.pdf#page=7"><text>VFWD 2017, Table 11 p.7</text></link>
    <sym>Fishing Area</sym>
    <type>b1_water</type>
  </wpt>
